Secondary material markets require stable demand to sustain investment in recovery infrastructure. Manufacturer commitments to recycled content create predictable demand supporting recycler business models. Recycled content policies close material loops by creating internal consumption of recovered materials.

Recycled content commitments reduce virgin material consumption, lowering environmental impacts and potentially improving cost economics as virgin material prices increase. Transparent recycled content targets hold manufacturers accountable for closing material loops. Consumer demand for recycled content-based products creates market differentiation and brand value.